;; hsi's divergences from GHC 9.14.1's -O0 runs (doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "As built: HE4a (write-ahead)"): the
;; classes every program of bin/hsi check that does not pass falls into, each with why and where it was decided, as
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's classes; a program is in the class whose :ids name it (bin/lib/hsi/check prints each
;; non-pass program's class, and fails on one in none). :kind :design is by design, :deferred is work a later
;; sub-step of HE4 or a later milestone owns (named). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :libm
  :title "libm's last bits: Go's math package in place of musl's libm"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "GHC's code calls the host's libm (musl 1.2.6) for exp, log, sin, cos, tan, the hyperbolic and inverse functions and pow, and their Float# variants (sinf, ...); hsi computes them with Go's math (the Float# ones in double, rounded): results differ in the last bit (exp 1.5, sinh 1.5, pow 1.5 -2.5, sin and cos of 1.0e308, the Float# trigonometry), and Go's amd64 log of a subnormal is wrong (log 5.0e-324 = -709.09, musl's -744.44). primops-double also prints decodeDouble_2Int# of 0.0's sign, which GHC's RTS leaves uninitialised (5719745 in the reference's run: a stack slot's leftover), an artefact no implementation reproduces"
  :decided "HES11 (a): libm through musl's C forms or a port of them, HE4b (HES37)"
  :ids ["synthetic/class-floating" "synthetic/primops-double" "synthetic/primops-float"]}
]
